	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/advanced/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Full draws the game at your screen's resolution. Above 100% draws it larger and scales it down: finer and smoother, for over twice the graphics card's work at 150%, four times at 200%. Xbox draws 640x480, scaled up: softer, and very light."/>
		<string text="Smooths jagged edges. FXAA and SMAA cost little; MSAA is sharper and costs more of the graphics card."/>
		<string text="Smooths jagged edges. FXAA and SMAA cost little; MSAA is sharper and costs more of the graphics card."/>
		<string text="Keeps floors and walls sharp into the distance, at a small cost. Off looks as the Xbox did: surfaces blur a few steps away."/>
		<string text="How detailed characters and vehicles stay in the distance. Xbox simplifies them as on a TV; Full keeps their detail for your screen; Highest always draws the most. Auto is Full in VR."/>
		<string text="Draws movement smoothly between the game's 30 updates a second, so that it looks fluid at any frame rate. Off shows each update as it is."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="How sharp the shadows of characters, vehicles and weapons are. Xbox is the original's soft, blocky shadow; each step up is crisper, and costs a little more of the graphics card."/>
		<string text="Lights characters and weapons smoothly, without the flat facets of the Xbox's lighting, at a small cost."/>
		<string text="Enhanced: plasma bolts, muzzle flashes and blasts light their surroundings smoothly, with a glow. Classic lights them as the Xbox did.|Classic for everyone in a Pro 2v2 game; yours again after it."/>
		<string text="World: soft shade where characters, vehicles and scenery meet the level and each other, from the level's shape; the levels keep their own lighting. Ray Traced: the shade of characters and vehicles traced by the graphics card, where it can (else World)."/>
		<string text="Shields light their surroundings as they flare, in the shield's own color. Online: the host's choice.|Off in Pro 2v2 games, for everyone."/>
		<string text="Light Show: the shields' glow reaches three times as far, and is brighter. Online: the host's choice.|Default in Pro 2v2 games, for everyone."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="How often the world updates each second, in games on this device (campaign, split screen, bots). 60 and 120 respond faster and take more of the processor. Online games play at their host's tick rate: a GOAT H1 game's (GOAT H1 60 Tick), a Legacy game's 30."/>
		<string text="Enhanced: you turn with your aim in a jump and a grenade throw, and your legs keep moving as you throw. Classic moves as the Xbox did, so the AI plays as it did. Online: the host's choice."/>
	</strings>
</menus>
